# Evidence

When you claim an external tool, package, library, or source exists, or that it does X, check it live in this run. Memory is only a hypothesis.

## Carry both

1. A live URL opened this run (docs, registry, repo, or release page).
2. A liveness signal: the date you checked, plus one freshness fact. Use last release, last commit, or "page reachable today".

Quote versions, pricing, limits, and license terms from that page, or leave them out.

## If you cannot check

Write `unverified: <claim>`.

Do not drop the claim silently. Do not state it as fact.

## Do not

- Recommend a name you only remember
- Invent a package, endpoint, or version to fill a gap
- Treat an example list inside a skill as a live check
